            "review_title": "Review at Phở Bò Ấu Triệu",
            "review_text": "Mark H\nPreston, United Kingdom98 contributions\n0\nAuthentic taste of Hanoi, breakfasting on Pho\nJan 2025 • Couples\nLooking for the authentic taste of Hanoi? Want to taste breakfast like the locals? Love eating tasty, delicious food? Then pull up a plastic stool and rub shoulders with people on their way to work in central Hanoi at this wonderful hole in the wall cafe near St Joseph’s cathedral. There is only one thing on the menu - pho. They cook the beef broth for ten hours, then add raw beef and herbs with rice noodles into the soupy mixture. The result is sublime. No wonder it’s so popular with a constant stream of people arriving from 6am. But get there early. Service is often finished by 10am when they have no more pho left to serve. Look for the charming chap standing outside on the street with a wad of notes in his hand when you leave to pay. Simply brilliant!\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nService is brisk but remember they only serve one thing. Bread is an optional extra. Be prepared to share a table\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten January 16, 2025",
